Subject: util: threads Mesa starts leave the hardware-fault signals unblocked

Mesa blocks every signal but SIGSYS and SIGSEGV on the threads it starts (u_thread_create_ex). On Darwin a hardware
fault whose signal is blocked on the faulting thread is not delivered: the thread runs the same instruction again
and faults again, forever, at full CPU (gpu/xnu-cpu-metal/test/faultmask.c shows it, on a Mac too). A protection
fault there is SIGBUS, not SIGSEGV, so a rasteriser thread that jumps to non-executable memory never ends its
process: iconservicesagent was seen at 100% of a CPU with 150,000 faults a second. With SIGBUS, SIGILL, SIGFPE and
SIGTRAP left unblocked the process dies with a crash report and launchd starts it again.

--- a/src/util/u_thread.c
+++ b/src/util/u_thread.c
@@ -84,6 +84,15 @@
     * that tracking mechanism.
     */
    sigdelset(&new_set, SIGSEGV);
+
+   /* A hardware fault on a thread that has its signal blocked is not delivered on Darwin: the thread takes the
+    * same fault again and again, at full CPU, and the process never dies (a protection fault there is SIGBUS,
+    * not SIGSEGV). Leave the fault signals to their default action.
+    */
+   sigdelset(&new_set, SIGBUS);
+   sigdelset(&new_set, SIGILL);
+   sigdelset(&new_set, SIGFPE);
+   sigdelset(&new_set, SIGTRAP);
    pthread_sigmask(SIG_BLOCK, &new_set, &saved_set);
    ret = thrd_create(thrd, thread_routine, paramp);
    pthread_sigmask(SIG_SETMASK, &saved_set, NULL);
